---
source: tests/cli_help.rs
expression: help_output(args)
---
Nag me about tasks: once a task's reminder is due, this machine notifies me every so often until it's completed

Only machines running the ms-todo daemon nag; the setting itself syncs with the task. A task needs a reminder to nag. Quiet hours (`[nag] quiet_hours`, 22:00-07:00 unless set) hold notifications back. `doctor --notify-test` checks notifications reach you

Usage: ms-todo tasks nag [OPTIONS] <--every <EVERY>|--off> <TASK>...

Arguments:
  <TASK>...
          Task IDs from `tasks list`, or exact titles when --list is given. `-` reads IDs from stdin, one per line

Options:
      --every <EVERY>
          How often: 15m, 1h, 1h30m (5m to 24h)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: jsonl is one object per line, ids one ID per line, csv has a header row [default: table in a terminal, json when piped]

          [possible values: table, json, jsonl, ids, csv]

      --instance <NAME>
          Use a separate copy of ms-todo's data (also MS_TODO_INSTANCE). Builds run from Cargo's target/ directory default to "dev"; "default" is the installed copy

      --off
          Stop nagging

      --fresh
          Before reading, sync and wait, so the answer is as fresh as Microsoft To Do's (a read is otherwise answered from the cache)

      --list <NAME|ID>
          Look for the tasks in this list (exact name or ID), which also lets TASK be an exact title

      --dry-run
          Show what would change without changing anything

      --quiet
          Print nothing on stderr but errors: no notes and no progress

      --no-color
          No colour or bold in tables (also NO_COLOR)

      --yes
          Change several tasks without asking. Off a terminal, changing more than one needs it

      --idempotency-key <KEY>
          Run this change at most once: repeating the command with the same key returns the first result for 24 hours, and the same key with a different change exits 2

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
